      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The cotton factory that defined Guilford ran from 1895 to 1916, starting with 50 looms in 1881 under James S. Gary and Son.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
